  "solution": "Logic : (1st number + 2nd number) = (3rd number + 9)\n\nGiven : \n\n \n• (44, 63, 98)\n\n44 + 63 = 98 + 9\n\n107 = 107 (LHS = RHS)\n\n \n• (59, 99, 149)\n\n59 + 99 = 149 + 9\n\n158 = 158 (LHS = RHS)\n\nSo,\n\n \n• Option - (1) : (81, 15, 87) \n\n81 + 15 = 87 + 9\n\n**96 = 96 (LHS = RHS)**\n\n \n• Option - (2) : (54, 73, 121) \n\n54 + 73 = 121 + 9\n\n127 ≠ 130 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\n \n• Option - (3) : (19, 32, 44) \n\n19 + 32 = 44 + 9\n\n51 ≠ 53 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\n \n• Option - (4) : (82, 13, 96) \n\n82 + 13 = 96 + 9\n\n95 ≠ 105 (LHS ≠ RHS) \n\nHence, \"Option - (1)\" is the correct answer.",
